"test8" COMMENTS
================

******************* Step to run this test *******************************

1. make -f makefile.man all

2. <testname>.sh 
Note: When running the script, the users will be asked to prepare 8 tapes and
      to load the first one.  Then the users will need to hit the return.  The 
      script will then perform "ms" (making the scrap tapes) and unload all the
      tapes.  This will take about 4 minutes.  The result scratch tapes will 
      have vol/serial number TEST01, TEST02, TEST03, TEST04, TEST11, TEST12,
      TEST13, TEST14 from bottom to top.  TEST01 to TEST04 will be used in 
      device label "/cfs/ctape0" and TEST11 to TEST14 will be used in device 
      label "/cfs/ctape1".  The user needs to load TEST01 and TEST11 in each
      device first and then hit RETURN to continue.  Afterward, the users will 
      need to feed the next tape (in serial number) when the device unloads a
      tape. 


      THE TEST TAKES ~30 MINUTES TO RUN




